SELECT - Select item(s) from a table.

SELECT [CONSISTENT] attribute_list | * FROM <table>[.<index>] [WHERE where_clause]
       [vector_search] [return_consumed_capacity|ratelimit]]

   vector_search := NEAREST <topk> TO [ number [, number ...] ]
      When <index> is a vector index (VSI), NEAREST routes the SELECT to a
      SearchVectors call: <topk> is the number of nearest items to return
      and the bracketed numeric list is the query vector (its length must
      equal the index DIMENSIONS). Each result row is shown with a trailing
      ` score <n>`. A WHERE clause becomes the search filter (it may
      reference only the vector index's HASH / FILTER search-key attributes).
      e.g. SELECT * FROM docs.embidx WHERE tenant = "acme" NEAREST 5 TO [0.1, 0.2, 0.3]

   where_clause := logical_element [AND|OR logical_element]
   logical_element := [NOT] logical_expression
   logical_element := ( logical_element )
   logical_element := lhs <comparison op> rhs
   logical_element := lhs BETWEEN bound AND bound
   logical_element := lhs IN ( list )
   logical_element := ATTRIBUTE_EXISTS (attribute)
   logical_element := ATTRIBUTE_TYPE (attribute, type)
   logical_element := BEGINS WITH (attribute, prefix)
   logical_element := CONTAINS (attribute, substring)
   logical_element := SIZE (attribute) <comparison op> NUMBER

   attribute_list - any attribute in the table, be it a scalar, boolean, null, list or map

   return_consumed_capacity := RETURN CONSUMED CAPACITY INDEXES | RETURN CONSUMED CAPACITY TOTAL

   ratelimit := WITH RATELIMIT ( RR RCU, WW WCU ) |
                WITH RATELIMIT ( RR RCU ) |
                WITH RATELIMIT ( WW WCU )

       NOTES: 1. The WHERE clause for a NULL field uses the SQL syntax of <field> IS [NOT] NULL
                 The equality operator cannot be used with NULL.
              2. To reference list elements in projection or where clause uses 0 based indexing.
              3. You can reference maps (dictionaries) in projection and where clause.
              4. You can rate limit a select by specifying the optional ratelimit parameter.
              5. You cannot specify both a rate limit and a return clause.

